'BluePerformance' is not a specific trim level but rather a technology package primarily found on BMW diesel engines to reduce nitrogen oxide (NOx) emissions using Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR) with AdBlue [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 20]. It has been available on various diesel models within the 3 Series range across different generations (like the F30 and current G20) [1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 10, 11, 13, 16, 17, 20, 22, 23].

To provide an evaluation, I will base the ratings on a representative recent BMW 3 Series diesel model equipped with BluePerformance. The G20 BMW 320d (produced since 2019, facelifted in 2022) is a common and recent example that features this technology [1, 4, 5, 7, 8, 12, 20, 24]. The evaluation below reflects the characteristics of the G20 320d with BluePerformance, focusing on the post-facelift (LCI) model where data is available.

